---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ShareButtons from '../components/ShareButtons.astro';

// Expanded from 3 questions to ~12 (content/faq-and-guides, item 1) — every
// answer below is grounded in content that already exists elsewhere on the
// site (mostly /india/law/, /quit/, /policy/ and /about/), nothing invented
// here. One question from the brief — "What is AVI's position on young
// people and vaping?" — is deliberately left out: the brief marked it
// "(I'll write this)", so it isn't AVI's place to draft it. See the PR
// description's "Needs Samrat" section.
//
// Each answer is plain prose (40-80 words, reused verbatim in the FAQPage
// JSON-LD below) plus a separate link to the full page it's drawn from —
// kept as a distinct field rather than inline markup so the JSON-LD
// `text` stays clean plain text.
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Is vaping illegal in India?',
    a: "No — not for personal use. India's Prohibition of Electronic Cigarettes Act, 2019 (PECA) bans the production, import, export, transport, sale, distribution, storage and advertisement of e-cigarettes — the business of them. Using, carrying or possessing a device for personal use isn't named as an offence anywhere in the Act, and no penalty attaches to it.",
    href: '/india/law/',
    linkText: 'Read the law in full →',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can police arrest or fine me for vaping?',
    a: 'No. PECA\'s penalties attach only to commercial acts — sale, production, import and the like — never to personal use or possession, so there\'s no legal basis for an arrest or an on-the-spot fine either. Officers who confiscate a device or demand cash "to settle it" are acting outside the law, not enforcing it.',
    href: '/india/law/#know-your-rights',
    linkText: 'Know your rights →',
  },
  {
    q: 'What should I do if police take my vape or ask for money?',
    a: 'Stay calm, and ask for the officer\'s name, badge number and station — a genuine officer gives this readily. Ask which law and section applies; there isn\'t one for personal use. Never hand over cash "to settle it" — that\'s a bribe, not a fine. If they push to confiscate your device, ask for a written seizure memo, then report what happened.',
    href: '/india/law/#know-your-rights',
    linkText: 'Full steps, and where to report it →',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I carry a vape on a flight in India?',
    a: 'Currently, no. The Bureau of Civil Aviation Security (BCAS) bans carrying e-cigarettes in checked or cabin baggage on Indian flights — a separate rule from PECA, with its own legal basis. AVI is challenging this in the Delhi High Court; judgment was reserved on 15 September 2026. Until that changes, devices carried on flights are liable to be confiscated at security.',
    href: '/litigation/delhi-bcas-flight-ban/',
    linkText: 'The flight-ban case →',
  },
  {
    q: 'Are nicotine pouches legal in India?',
    a: "No law names or bans nicotine pouches, but as of September 2026 there's no lawful route to sell them either. FSSAI's food rules bar nicotine as an ingredient, and an August 2026 drug-approval freeze closed the other route. It's a regulatory freeze, not an Act of Parliament — the same kind of overreach courts rejected for e-cigarettes in 2019.",
    href: '/india/nicotine-pouches/',
    linkText: 'The full breakdown →',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does PECA cover heated tobacco products?',
    a: 'Yes. PECA\'s own definition of "electronic cigarette" explicitly includes "all forms of Electronic Nicotine Delivery Systems, Heat Not Burn Products, e-Hookah and the like devices, by whatever name called." So heated tobacco products face the same bans on sale, import and advertisement as vapes — and personal use isn\'t banned for them either, for the same reason it isn\'t for e-cigarettes.',
    href: '/india/law/',
    linkText: 'Read the Act itself →',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is vaping safer than smoking?',
    a: "Yes. Major health bodies agree it's the burning of tobacco, not the nicotine, that causes most smoking-related disease, and vaping involves no combustion. Cochrane's living review found nicotine e-cigarettes help more smokers quit than nicotine replacement therapy — about 8–10 per 100 vapers, against 6 per 100 using gums or patches.",
    href: '/quit/#does-it-work',
    linkText: 'See the evidence →',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does vaping help smokers quit?',
    a: "The best available evidence says yes. Cochrane's 2025 living review found about 8–10 smokers per 100 quit using nicotine e-cigarettes, against 6 with nicotine replacement therapy and 4 with no support at all — making e-cigarettes the most effective cessation aid studied head-to-head so far.",
    href: '/quit/#does-it-work',
    linkText: 'The full evidence →',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is nicotine what makes smoking dangerous?',
    a: "No. The overwhelming evidence, summarised by bodies including the UK's Royal College of Physicians, is that it's burning tobacco — the tar and thousands of combustion byproducts — that causes most smoking-related disease, not the nicotine itself. That's the basis for why switching to a non-combustible nicotine source lowers risk so sharply.",
    href: '/quit/#what-matters',
    linkText: 'More on what the evidence says →',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who funds AVI, and does it take industry money?',
    a: 'AVI accepts no funding from tobacco or nicotine manufacturers. Domestic contributions supporting its advocacy are received and accounted for through Harm Reduction Policy & Research (HRPR), audited annually and taxed as company income. Overseas support is handled only as contracted, invoiced project work — not through this site.',
    href: '/about/#funding',
    linkText: 'How AVI is funded and governed →',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is AVI a registered organisation?',
    a: "No — AVI itself is not a registered legal entity. Domestic contributions supporting its work are received and accounted for through Harm Reduction Policy & Research (HRPR), a private limited company registered with India's Ministry of Corporate Affairs, audited annually rather than held in a personal account.",
    href: '/about/#funding',
    linkText: 'More on how AVI is governed →',
  },
];

const faqLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map((f) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: f.q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: f.a },
  })),
};
---
<Base
  title="Vaping in India: FAQ"
  description="Quick, sourced answers on vaping law, nicotine pouches, flight rules and the evidence on switching — is it illegal, can police fine you, does it help you quit."
  image="/og/faq.png"
  wide={true}
>
  {/* Astro's layout doesn't expose a <head> slot (Base.astro's <head> is
      fixed), so this JSON-LD renders as the first element of <body>/<main>
      instead — the same place /india/law and /quit already put their own
      FAQPage schema. Google explicitly supports JSON-LD anywhere in the
      HTML, body included, and this project's existing FAQ-schema pages are
      already verified working in Search Console on that basis. */}
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqLd)} />

  <section class="breakout faq-hero">
    <div class="breakout-inner">
      <p class="eyebrow">Quick answers</p>
      <h1>Vaping in India: FAQ</h1>
      <p class="faq-sub">Short, direct answers to the questions people search for most — each one sourced and linking to the full page behind it.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="faq-body">
    <div class="faq-share">
      <ShareButtons title="Vaping in India: FAQ — quick, sourced answers" />
    </div>
    <div class="faq-accordion">
      {faqs.map((f, i) => (
        <details class="faq-item" open={i === 0}>
          <summary>{f.q}</summary>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>{f.a}</p>
            <p class="faq-link"><a href={f.href}>{f.linkText}</a></p>
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div class="faq-related">
      <a href="/india/law/" class="related-card">
        <h3>The full legal breakdown →</h3>
        <p>Every detail on what PECA bans, with government sources and what to do if you're stopped.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/litigation/delhi-bcas-flight-ban/" class="related-card">
        <h3>The flight-ban case →</h3>
        <p>AVI's ongoing Delhi High Court challenge to the BCAS carry-on restriction.</p>
      </a>
      <a href="/report-harassment/" class="related-card">
        <h3>Report police harassment →</h3>
        <p>Stopped or shaken down over vaping, even though it's not banned? Log it.</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <style>
    .eyebrow {
      font-size: 0.82rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.08em;
      color: var(--gold-light);
      margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
    }
    .faq-hero {
      background: linear-gradient(rgba(18,19,15,0.85), rgba(18,19,15,0.93)), url('/images/backgrounds/open-sky.jpg');
      background-size: cover;
      background-position: center;
      color: #f4f1e6;
      padding: 3.25rem 0 2.75rem;
    }
    .faq-hero h1 { color: #fff; margin: 0 0 0.85rem; font-size: clamp(1.9rem, 3.6vw, 2.6rem); }
    .faq-sub { color: #cdd6cf; max-width: 36rem; font-size: 1.02rem; margin: 0; }

    .faq-body { max-width: var(--max-w); margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.75rem 1.5rem 4rem; }

    .faq-share { margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
    .faq-accordion { display: grid; gap: 0.85rem; margin-bottom: 2.5rem; }
    .faq-item {
      background: #fff;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 10px;
      padding: 0 1.25rem;
    }
    .faq-item summary {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 1rem;
      padding: 1.1rem 0;
      cursor: pointer;
      list-style: none;
      font-weight: 600;
      font-size: 1.02rem;
      color: var(--ink);
    }
    .faq-item summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
    .faq-item summary::after { content: '▾'; font-size: 0.85em; color: var(--muted); flex-shrink: 0; transition: transform 0.15s ease; }
    .faq-item[open] summary::after { transform: rotate(180deg); }
    .faq-answer { padding: 0 0 1.25rem; }
    .faq-answer p { margin: 0 0 0.75rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.65; }
    .faq-answer p.faq-link { margin: 0; font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 600; }
    .faq-answer p.faq-link a { text-decoration: none; }
    .faq-answer p.faq-link a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

    .faq-related {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(14rem, 100%), 1fr));
      gap: 1.25rem;
      padding-top: 2rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .related-card {
      display: block;
      text-decoration: none;
      color: inherit;
      background: var(--paper-alt);
      border-radius: 8px;
      padding: 1.25rem 1.4rem;
      transition: transform 0.15s ease;
    }
    .related-card:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); }
    .related-card h3 { margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: 1rem; color: var(--accent-dark); }
    .related-card p { margin: 0; font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.5; }
  </style>
</Base>
